;; The cases the per-form differential check (bin/diffcheck; doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, "F2 as
;; built") leaves out of both runs, with the reasons: cases the back end and j2g cannot compile,
;; so that the rest of their corpus file is compiled (arbace.aot compiles a source whole or not at
;; all, and j2g's errors stop the build). Each becomes (diffcheck.driver/excluded* ID FILE): a
;; later case that depends on it fails alike in both runs. Named FILE:LINE, as the oracle names
;; cases.
{:excluded
 [{:reason "j2g: Go names collide (J2G-SPEC §4.4, reported as an error): a reify inside an anonymous fn inside a fn (here the case's own fn) is named X$fn__N$fn$reify__M, so its declaring class X$fn__N$fn gets the Go variable X_fn__N_fn_class, the Go name of the static field fn-class of the code class X$fn__N (SA154). The runtime's namespaces have no such reify"
   :cases ["test/oracle/forms/concurrency.ae:106" "test/oracle/forms/concurrency.ae:223"
           "test/oracle/forms/concurrency.ae:244" "test/oracle/forms/concurrency.ae:364"]}

  {:reason "The back end names a proxy's class as a class of the program when its analysis finds the class made already, at run time: case 12 makes the proxy class of Object by (get-proxy-class Object) when it runs, so case 13's (proxy [Object] [] ...) records no proxy event and its compiled code names dcf.harvest.java_interop.proxy$java.lang.Object$ff19274a directly, a class j2g does not have (Unable to resolve class)"
   :cases ["test/oracle/forms/harvest/java_interop.ae:13"]}]}
